questions.q:
Consider the following test for a group-IV cation.
$\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{M}^{2+}+\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{ S} \rightarrow \mathrm{A} \text{ (Black precipitate) }+ \text{ by product } \\
& \mathrm{A}+\text{ aqua regia } \rightarrow \mathrm{B}+\mathrm{NOCl}+\mathrm{S}+\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O} \\
& \mathrm{B}+\mathrm{KNO}_2+\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{COOH} \rightarrow \mathrm{C}+\text{ by product }
\end{aligned}\)$ The $spin-only magnetic moment value of the metal complex \(\mathrm{C}\) is ______ BM (Nearest integer)$

