questions.solution:
$\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{NH}_4 \mathrm{OH} \rightleftharpoons \mathrm{NH}_4^{+}+\mathrm{OH}^{-} \\
& \mathrm{NH}_4 \mathrm{Cl} \rightarrow \mathrm{NH}_4^{+}+\mathrm{Cl}
\end{aligned}$<br />Due to common ion effect of $\mathrm{NH}_4^{+}$,
$\left[\mathrm{OH}^{-}\right]$decreases in such extent that only group-III cation can be precipitated, due to their very low $\mathrm{K}_{\mathrm{sp}}$ in the range of $10^{-38}$.

